From fcc80cce99d7bdc01e5d6201e5f5012a2ab9767c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:35:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 18/51] diag: MEGALON_DIAG writer record-ownership check,
 last-Get path on value-check failure, post-stop watchdog

G-B v2.9 r1-P-rev64 (reclaim pressure): torn reads that passed validation, then a hang after stop.
Hypothesis: a writer locks a record that reclaim has meanwhile switched away from its key and reused
(RO switch emits no change notification), then writes a key that readers now read on the RO path.
With MEGALON_DIAG=1 the writer re-reads the GCD entry after locking (and, in artifact64, compares the
record's BlockId) and counts mismatches without changing behaviour; a failed value check prints the
Get's path/record/seq; KV_WATCHDOG_S also covers workers stuck after stop. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
